        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "(1) New Employees – With respect to new employees, the first three hundred and sixty-five (365) calendar days of employment shall be considered a probationary period during which time such employee shall not be placed on the seniority list. During the first one-hundred and eighty (180) calendar days of employment, an employee may be discharged without recourse to the grievance procedure. During the entire probationary period of three hundred sixty-five (365) calendar days, an employee can also be discharged without recourse to the grievance procedure if the employee is not qualified for the position or has failed to demonstrate satisfactory job performance. After completion of the probationary period, such new employee's seniority shall start from the date of hiring.",
            "block_bbox": [
                96,
                119,
                675,
                364
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 2,
            "block_polygon_points": [
